	(text "3. Selecting the Precision ADC\nTo capture <1µV signals, you need a 24-bit or 32-bit Delta-Sigma ADC. The standard 12-bit or 16-bit SAR ADCs used in microcontrollers will not see the signal floor you have created.\n\nTop Recommendations:\n\nTI ADS1261 (24-bit / 32-bit mode):\n\nWhy: It has a built-in PGA (Programmable Gain Amplifier) that is extremely low noise.\n\nNoise Floor: Can resolve down to ~6 nV RMS at low data rates.\n\nAnalog Devices AD7177-2 (32-bit):\n\nWhy: True 32-bit output with a 10 kSPS rate. Excellent for DC precision."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.275 -25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "047f5d2f-b0a8-4d18-b5e3-b20a102b692f")
	)
